{"case_id":"C059","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","input semantics","API protocol"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["solidity::langutil::EVMVersion::paris","solidity::langutil::EVMVersion::fromString","solidity::langutil::EVMVersion::name","FuzzerUtil::testCompilerJsonInterface","FuzzerUtil::testCompiler","ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping"],"reason":"S1 introduces the selectable EVM version \"paris\", but H0's structured compiler and Yul paths cannot select it. Consequently, Paris-specific version parsing and compilation behavior lack deliberate fuzz coverage.","evidence":["EVMVersion::fromString now recognizes paris(), and EVMVersion::name returns \"paris\" for Version::Paris.","FuzzerUtil::testCompilerJsonInterface hard-codes config[\"settings\"][\"evmVersion\"] = \"berlin\".","FuzzerUtil::testCompiler selects from s_evmVersions, whose latest entry is EVMVersion::berlin().","ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping handles Program versions only through Program::BERLIN and has no Paris case.","The command-line --evm-version description now advertises \"paris\", exposing the new configuration to users."],"recommended_action":"Add Paris to s_evmVersions and to the protobuf Program_Version plus ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping; also allow testCompilerJsonInterface to fuzz or explicitly exercise settings.evmVersion=\"paris\" and validate accepted/rejected version strings through the relevant compiler interface."}
